# Batch steps assume ingredients are in the state printed on the card.
notes = {
0:('10 min + overnight','Set out 3 or 4 jars. Divide oats and yogurt evenly. Mash half the banana into each jar, close and chill overnight. Slice the remaining banana just before eating.','Keep jars cold. Use within 3 days. For breakfast 4, measure dry oats now and add yogurt and banana the night before.'),
1:('18–25 min','Make the oat and banana filling in one bowl. Divide between 3 or 4 tortillas. Fold each over. Toast in pairs if they fit, 2 minutes on each side.','Chill folds in a single layer, then box them. Keep the yogurt dip separate. Warm one fold in a dry pan before eating.'),
2:('10–15 min','Line up 3 or 4 small boxes. Divide the sliced chicken and dry lettuce between them. Pack yogurt and cucumber on the side. Keep the tortillas in their bag.','Keep fillings cold. Roll one wrap before work and refrigerate it until your break.'),
3:('20–30 min','Soften all the peppers together. Divide peppers, cooked chicken and rice among shallow boxes. If packing for later, skip the final pan heat. Pack garlic yogurt separately.','Reheat one box to 74°C, stir, then add the cold yogurt.'),
4:('15–20 min','Put the chilled pasta and chicken into 3 or 4 boxes. Grate the carrots and divide them among the boxes. Mix one batch of mustard yogurt and portion it into small pots.','Chill everything. Add cucumber and dressing just before eating so the salad stays crisp.'),
5:('15–20 min','Grate all the carrots, chop the cooked chicken and pat the lettuce dry. Measure one set of fillings per tortilla. Keep the hummus in small cups.','Keep fillings cold. Roll one tortilla the morning you need it, then slice into four rounds.'),
6:('15–25 min','Cook all the corn in the measured oil. Portion it with chicken, cooked rice and soy sauce. To serve now, stir-fry in batches so everything heats evenly.','For later, chill the boxes promptly and reheat one to 74°C with a splash of water.'),
7:('20–25 min','Mash the beans and lemon in one bowl. Divide the mash, cooked pasta and chicken among shallow boxes. Portion the garlic yogurt separately.','Reheat one box to 74°C with a spoonful of water, stir, then add the yogurt.'),
8:('25–45 min','Shape 9 short kofta logs for 3 plates or 12 for 4 plates. Oil and air-fry in single layers. Check each load reaches 71°C. Box 3 logs with each rice portion.','Keep cucumber yogurt in its own cup. Reheat one hot portion to 74°C, then add the cold dip.'),
9:('20–30 min','Slice all the peppers first. Brown the beef in two pan loads if crowded. Check each load reaches 71°C. Toss with the peppers, cooked pasta and the measured soy sauce.','Divide into shallow boxes. Reheat one to 74°C with a splash of water to loosen the pasta.'),
10:('30–40 min','Halve and soften the peppers in microwave-safe batches. Brown the beef to 71°C. Stir in the rice. Divide the peppers and filling among boxes and portion hummus separately.','Reheat peppers and filling to 74°C. Spoon hummus into each pepper, then add the filling.'),
11:('20–30 min','Brown all the beef to 71°C, in two pan loads if needed. Stir in the beans, corn and mustard. Split the filling evenly. Dry the lettuce leaves and cut the tortillas into wedges.','Pack filling, lettuce and tortilla wedges separately. Reheat filling to 74°C and spoon into leaves.'),
12:('25–35 min','Make 6 small patties for 3 meals or 8 for 4. Cook in one layer per pan load to 71°C. Brush with mustard. Divide chilled pasta, dressing and cucumber for the sides.','Pack two patties per box. Keep pasta salad cold while reheating patties to 74°C.'),
13:('25–40 min','Brown the beef to 71°C. Mash the beans. Spread one share of beans, corn and beef on each tortilla and fold. Toast in batches using the total oil in your chosen column.','Chill the pockets in shallow boxes. Reheat one to 74°C and crisp briefly in a dry pan.'),
14:('15–20 min','Drain tuna and corn well. Mix the mustard and yogurt in a cup. Divide chilled pasta, flaked tuna and corn between boxes. Portion dressing and cucumber separately.','Keep cold. Add cucumber and dressing, close the box and shake gently before lunch.'),
15:('15–20 min','Grate the carrots. Mix with drained tuna and hummus in one bowl. Divide into 3 or 4 covered cups. Cut the tortilla wedges and pack dry.','Chill the filling. Cut and hollow a fresh cucumber portion on the day you eat it. Spoon in one cup of filling.'),
16:('15–20 min','Divide cooked rice between shallow boxes. Drain and divide tuna. Peel the carrot ribbons and cut cucumber sticks. Measure soy sauce and oil into small cups.','Keep tuna, vegetables and dressing cold and separate. Thaw frozen rice in the fridge. Assemble when ready to eat.'),
17:('15–25 min','Make one bowl of bean mash. Divide it and the drained tuna into small cups. Slice the peppers. Toast the tortillas in a dry pan, then cool and pack dry.','Keep tuna, mash and peppers cold. Spread and top one tortilla just before eating.'),
18:('25–40 min','Mash all chickpeas and oats. Make 9 small patties for 3 wraps or 12 for 4. Cook in one layer per pan load, using the total measured oil. Cool in shallow boxes.','Pack 3 patties per meal. Keep lettuce and yogurt cold. Roll the tortilla just before eating.'),
19:('15–20 min','Grate the carrots. Heat with chickpeas and cooked penne in a large pan. Stir the hummus, lemon and warm water together. Toss with the pasta and divide into boxes.','Reheat one box to 74°C. Add a spoonful of water and stir to loosen the hummus sauce.'),
20:('20–30 min','Soften the diced peppers in a wide pan. Stir in beans, corn and rice. Mash some beans and divide the filling among shallow boxes. Portion yogurt separately.','Reheat one filling portion to 74°C. Add yogurt, fill one tortilla and roll.'),
21:('20–30 min','Microwave grated carrots in batches until soft. Add beans, lemon and oil and mash. Divide dip evenly. Toast tortillas, cut into strips and cool before packing dry.','Chill the dip and cucumber sticks separately. Scoop the dip with tortilla strips just before eating.'),
22:('15–25 min','Rinse beans and drain corn. Divide among boxes. Shake lemon juice and oil together in a jar. Toast the tortillas, cut into triangles and pack dry.','Keep beans, cucumber and lettuce chilled. Add dressing and tortilla triangles at the table.'),
23:('25–45 min','Oil the peppers and chickpeas. Air-fry in one layer per load, shaking halfway. Portion with cooked rice. Mix the hummus and lemon into a dip and pack it separately.','Reheat one rice box to 74°C, then add the cold hummus dressing.'),
24:('1¾–2 hr from raw','Roast one whole bird using the oven guide, or buy a plain cooked bird. Carve and weigh 450 g edible meat for 3 plates or 600 g for 4. Put 150 g meat in each box with its rice.','Pack the cucumber and lemon yogurt separately. Reheat the chicken and rice to 74°C, then add the cold sides.'),
25:('18–28 min','Shape 3 or 4 patties, each from 75 g raw beef. Cook in a single layer, in two pan loads if needed. Check the middle of every patty reaches 71°C. Cool in shallow boxes.','Pack the buns dry and chill the toppings separately. Reheat one patty to 74°C, then build one burger.'),
26:('1 min','Choose 3 or 4 bananas. Each portion is about 120 g peeled. Leave them whole and unpeeled until gym time.','Keep whole bananas on the counter. If they ripen early, peel and freeze in single portions.')}
